00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:33.740
<v M. Gessen>David, though, is much more interested in the bribe part. In court, he testified that he went to the meeting expecting to talk about the deportation scheme, not the factory, but he is nimble. He tells Allen that he could bring in money from the Colombian drug cartels to invest in the factory. Remember, the FBI has been trying for years to get Kisolov and now Allen on money laundering. But Allen isn't really incriminating himself. He actually expresses some concerns about the drug money.
<v M. Gessen>不过，大卫对行贿部分更感兴趣。在法庭上，他作证说他去开会时以为是来谈驱逐出境计划的，而不是工厂，但他随机应变能力很强。他告诉艾伦，他可以引入哥伦比亚贩毒集团的资金来投资这家工厂。记住，FBI多年来一直试图以洗钱罪逮捕基索洛夫，现在则是艾伦。但艾伦并没有真正自证其罪。他实际上对毒品资金表达了一些担忧。

00:43:33.740 --> 00:43:56.840
<v M. Gessen>After an hour or so, the conversation turns back to Priscilla. Allen says, quote, "the first order of business is to get her the fuck out of here," end quote. To get Priscilla deported, or-- and this is where he suddenly, offhandedly, turns the conversation in a different direction. This is the heart of the prosecution's case. Let's listen carefully.
<v M. Gessen>大约一个小时后，谈话重新回到了普莉希拉身上。艾伦说，引述原话，“首要任务是把她他妈的弄出这儿”，引述结束。为了把普莉希拉驱逐出境，或者——也就是在这里，他突然漫不经心地把谈话引向了一个不同的方向。这就是控方证据的核心。让我们仔细听听。

00:43:56.840 --> 00:43:57.580
<v David>Yeah.
<v David>对。

00:43:57.580 --> 00:44:00.300
<v Allen>Incidentally, if there's a cheaper way to get rid of her, I'm happy to do it, of course.
<v Allen>顺便说一句，如果有更便宜的方法能除掉她，我当然很乐意这么做。

00:44:00.300 --> 00:44:02.860
<v M. Gessen>If there's a cheaper way to get rid of her.
<v M. Gessen>如果有更便宜的方法能除掉她。

00:44:02.860 --> 00:44:09.940
<v David>I mean, listen, I have family in your area.
<v David>我的意思是，听着，我在你们地区有家人。

00:44:09.940 --> 00:44:25.900
<v M. Gessen>Remember, David is supposed to be a mafioso. That's the kind of family he's talking about. A minute later, he will refer to friends in the North End, historically an Italian neighborhood in Boston. He is opening, for Allen, a door to the underworld.
<v M. Gessen>记住，大卫应该扮演一个黑手党成员。这就是他所说的“家人”的意思。一分钟后，他会提到在北区（North End）的朋友，北区在历史上是波士顿的一个意大利人聚居区。他正在为艾伦打开一扇通往地下世界的大门。

00:44:25.900 --> 00:44:35.180
<v David>So, I don't know how to say this, but there is a cheaper way and probably a more permanent way to do it, but--
<v David>所以，我不知道该怎么说，但有一个更便宜、可能也更永久的方法可以做到这一点，不过——

00:44:35.180 --> 00:44:39.780
<v M. Gessen>A more permanent way. In case Allen didn't understand what David was getting at--
<v M. Gessen>一种更彻底的方法。万一艾伦没听懂大卫的暗示——

00:44:39.780 --> 00:44:40.360
<v Allen>She's dead.
<v Allen>她死掉。

00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:42.900
<v David>Yeah. I mean, that's up to you.
<v David>对。我的意思是，这取决于你。

00:44:42.900 --> 00:44:45.380
<v Allen>Uh, I would like to proceed.
<v Allen>呃，我想继续进行。

00:44:45.380 --> 00:44:46.680
<v M. Gessen>Allen would like to proceed.
<v M. Gessen>艾伦想要继续进行。

00:44:46.680 --> 00:44:47.180
<v David>That route?
<v David>走那条路？

00:44:47.180 --> 00:44:49.620
<v Allen>Yeah.
<v Allen>对。

00:44:49.620 --> 00:45:13.180
<v M. Gessen>The time that elapses between the agent saying, "that's up to you" and Allen's agreement to "proceed" with the more permanent option is a fraction of a second. He doesn't take a breath. He doesn't pretend to consider the decision. He doesn't double check that he understood the agent correctly. He doesn't even ask how much money he'll save by going for the cheaper option. He jumps right in with both feet.
<v M. Gessen>卧底特工说“这取决于你”与艾伦同意“继续”采用那个更一劳永逸的方案之间，间隔的时间只有零点几秒。他没有深吸一口气。他没有假装考虑这个决定。他没有再次确认自己是否听懂了特工的话。他甚至没有问选择便宜的方案能省多少钱。他毫不犹豫地一头扎了进去。

00:45:13.180 --> 00:45:40.260
<v M. Gessen>And then it gets worse. Allen says that he had looked into this more permanent option before, that he talked to Israelis, and Eastern Europeans, and Italians, and the lowest estimate he got was $220,000. The prosecutor stopped the tape and repeated what Allen had said. "I researched my sources. The lowest price was 220. And then that is run through the Israelis and Eastern Europe and Italy."
<v M. Gessen>然后情况更糟了。艾伦说他以前了解过这个更一劳永逸的方案，他跟以色列人、东欧人和意大利人谈过，他得到的最低报价是22万美元。检察官暂停了录音，重复了艾伦说过的话。“我调查过我的渠道。最低价格是22万。然后这通过以色列人、东欧和意大利人来操作。”

00:45:40.260 --> 00:46:01.700
<v M. Gessen>She asked the undercover agent what he had understood Allen to be saying. The agent answered, "my understanding was that Mr. Gessen had already researched the option to kill his wife and had been in conversation, or had done some research with other organized crime syndicates, in this case Israelis or Eastern Europe, for the price of $220,000."
<v M. Gessen>她问卧底特工，他当时理解艾伦在说些什么。特工回答说：“我的理解是，盖森先生已经研究过杀害他妻子的方案，并且已经跟其他有组织犯罪集团沟通过，或者做过一些调查，在这个案子里是以色列人或东欧人，价格是22万美元。”

00:46:01.700 --> 00:46:10.660
<v M. Gessen>The agent, who had worked on murder-for-hire cases before, testified in court that it was cheap. He'd seen people agree to kill someone for as little as $200.
<v M. Gessen>这位处理过谋杀雇凶案的特工在法庭上作证说，这很便宜。他见过有人答应杀一个人只要200美元。

00:46:10.660 --> 00:46:12.140
<v David>If that's what you want you have to tell me.
<v David>如果你想要那个，你得告诉我。

00:46:12.140 --> 00:46:29.300
<v M. Gessen>On the tape, David assures Allen that his friends on the north end are more dependable and affordable than those other guys, the Israelis or the Eastern Europeans, and adds that they can get the job done quickly. Allen likes this, and he clarifies, more definite.
<v M. Gessen>在录音中，大卫向艾伦保证，他在北区的那些朋友比其他人——那些以色列人或东欧人——更靠谱、更实惠，并补充说他们能快刀斩乱麻。艾伦很喜欢这样，他明确指出，要更明确。

00:46:29.300 --> 00:46:31.300
<v Allen>And more-- and more definite.
<v Allen>而且更——更明确。

00:46:31.300 --> 00:46:33.460
<v David>Permanent.
<v David>一劳永逸。

00:46:33.460 --> 00:46:47.180
<v M. Gessen>The prosecutor asked, "when you heard Mr. Gessen say, and more definite, what was your understanding of that?" The agent answered, "more definite is permanent, dead."
<v M. Gessen>检察官问：“当你听到盖森先生说‘更明确’时，你的理解是什么？”特工回答说：“更明确就是一劳永逸，死。”

00:46:47.180 --> 00:47:06.260
<v M. Gessen>I'd seen FBI agents testify in court before. Often I've been skeptical. Their interpretations of what people say to them can be far-fetched. Their entrapment techniques are often crude and mendacious. I've seen cases where the undercover agent talks a person into a crime they had no intention of committing. But this was different.
<v M. Gessen>我以前在法庭上见过联邦调查局特工作证。我经常持怀疑态度。他们对别人对他们说的话的解读有时会很牵强。他们的诱捕手段通常也很粗糙、虚伪。我见过卧底特工劝说某人去犯罪，而那个人本无意犯罪。但这次不一样。

00:47:06.260 --> 00:47:24.980
<v M. Gessen>I couldn't imagine any alternative interpretation of the tape I'd just heard. Allen wanted Priscilla killed, and he wanted David to know that he wanted Priscilla killed. He said that with the bribery scheme, he was worried that Priscilla could fight her deportation in court and maybe even win. Murder is better than deportation that way.
<v M. Gessen>对于我刚刚听到的录音，我想不出任何别的解释。艾伦想让普莉西拉去死，而且他想让大卫知道他想让普莉西拉去死。他说，相比于贿赂计划，他担心普莉西拉会在法庭上抗争她的驱逐令，甚至可能赢。从这个角度来看，谋杀比驱逐出境更好。

00:47:24.980 --> 00:47:40.980
<v David>Of course, that's-- we could handle that. I just didn't know what your appetite for that was. But if you feel that way we can make that happen. It will be very clean, it'll be quick, and it will be final. But you gotta tell me if that's the route that you want to take.
<v David>当然，那是——我们可以处理。我只是不知道你对那种事的胃口有多大。但如果你有这种感觉，我们可以把它变成现实。它会非常干净利落，会很快，而且是最终结果。但你必须告诉我，这是不是你想选的路线。

00:47:40.980 --> 00:47:45.740
<v Allen>My single concern is, I need to be sure that you cannot possibly [? hurt ?] the kids.
<v Allen>我唯一的顾虑是，我需要确定你们绝对不会[？伤害？]孩子们。

00:47:45.740 --> 00:47:46.740
<v David>No.
<v David>不。

00:47:46.740 --> 00:47:52.420
<v M. Gessen>This is the only thing that gives Allen pause. He doesn't want the kids to see their mother getting killed.
<v M. Gessen>这是唯一让艾伦犹豫不决的事情。他不想让孩子们看到他们的母亲被杀。

00:47:52.420 --> 00:47:59.000
<v David>No, no, no. God, please. Yeah, no, no. No, we're all family men. Like, this is strictly business.
<v David>不，不，不。天哪，拜托。对，不，不。不，我们都是有家室的男人。就像，这纯粹是生意。

00:47:59.000 --> 00:48:07.160
<v Allen>OK, because that was my one concern with that route is that I want to make sure that whoever does this, will make sure it's--
<v Allen>好吧，因为那是我对那条路线唯一的顾虑，我想确保做这件事的人，会确保它——

00:48:07.160 --> 00:48:12.220
<v David>No, no, no, no, no, no. No. This would be a very clean, professional job.
<v David>不，不，不，不，不，不。不。这将是一份非常干净利落、专业的工作。

00:48:12.220 --> 00:48:15.380
<v M. Gessen>Reassured, Allen asks about the cost.
<v M. Gessen>吃下定心丸后，艾伦打听起费用来。

00:48:15.380 --> 00:48:19.200
<v David>I think it's probably half the cost, to tell you the truth. Yeah.
<v David>说实话，我觉得这大概是一半的费用。对。

00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:20.840
<v Allen>It's much easier, much easier.
<v Allen>容易得多，容易得多。

00:48:20.840 --> 00:48:21.340
<v David>OK.
<v David>好吧。

00:48:21.340 --> 00:48:22.620
<v Allen>Very happy to proceed with it.
<v Allen>很高兴继续进行。

00:48:22.620 --> 00:48:23.460
<v David>OK.
<v David>好吧。

00:48:23.460 --> 00:48:29.260
<v M. Gessen>"Very happy to proceed with it."
<v M. Gessen>“很高兴继续进行。”

00:48:29.260 --> 00:48:56.340
<v M. Gessen>What a productive meeting for the undercover agent. He came for bribery and was leaving with murder for hire. Now he just needed Allen to confirm that he intended to go through with it so that when Allen eventually went to trial, he couldn't say that he was misunderstood. And now, here we were at that trial, listening to and looking at all the times and all the ways Allen said that, yes, he really meant it. He wanted Priscilla killed.
<v M. Gessen>对卧底特工来说，这是一次多么富有成效的会面啊。他本来是来查贿赂的，结果却接下了雇凶杀人的活儿。现在他只需要艾伦确认他打算把这事进行到底，这样当艾伦最终受审时，他就不能说自己被误解了。现在，我们来到了那场审判中，听着并看着艾伦说“是的，他是认真的”所有时刻和所有方式。他想要普莉西拉去死。

00:48:56.340 --> 00:48:59.340
<v David>Well, you have to be sure that this is what you're-- OK, all right.
<v David>好吧，你得确定这就是你所——好吧，行吧。

00:48:59.340 --> 00:49:06.800
<v M. Gessen>This is the first time. The agent asks Allen if he is sure. And Allen says, "I'm sure." And he adds--
<v M. Gessen>这是第一次。特工问艾伦是不是确信。艾伦说：“我很确信。”他还补充说——

00:49:06.800 --> 00:49:08.190
<v Allen>I'm sure.
<v Allen>我很确信。

00:49:08.190 --> 00:49:09.390
<v M. Gessen>I'm sure.
<v M. Gessen>我很确信。

00:49:09.390 --> 00:49:11.480
<v Allen>This is not like a spur of the moment or emotional reaction.
<v Allen>这不像是头脑发热或情绪化的反应。

00:49:11.480 --> 00:49:22.150
<v David>No, no, no. This sounds like it's been well thought out. Listen yeah, I didn't want to-- I'm glad we talked about it, because that's-- honestly, that's the way I would have handled it. But that's the-- you gotta be comfortable with it, right?
<v David>不，不，不。这听起来经过了深思熟虑。听着，对，我不想——我很高兴我们谈了谈，因为那是——老实说，这就是我会处理的方式。但那是——你得对此感到自在，对吧？

00:49:22.150 --> 00:49:22.650
<v Allen>I'm comfortable.
<v Allen>我很自在。

00:49:22.530 --> 00:49:25.350
<v David>OK, good. All right.
<v David>好的，很好。行。

00:49:25.350 --> 00:49:30.450
<v M. Gessen>Allen says that this is not an emotional decision, not spur of the moment. He is comfortable with it.
<v M. Gessen>艾伦说这不是一个情绪化的决定，也不是一时冲动。他对此感到心安。

00:49:30.450 --> 00:49:32.750
<v David>Sometimes they dig their own fucking grave.
<v David>有时他们是在自掘他妈的坟墓。

00:49:32.750 --> 00:49:33.250
<v Allen>Don't fuck with me.
<v Allen>别跟我耍花招。

00:49:33.230 --> 00:49:34.230
<v David>Right, yeah.
<v David>对，没错。

00:49:34.230 --> 00:49:48.230
<v M. Gessen>"Don't fuck with me." There's a bit more back and forth. David will need pictures of Priscilla, location, everything for the people who'll do the job. And then, just like that, Allen is showing David pictures of the kids.
<v M. Gessen>“别跟我耍花招。”还有一些来来回回的对话。大卫需要普莉西拉的照片、地址，以及执行任务的人所需要的一切。然后，就这样，艾伦开始向大卫展示孩子们的照片。

00:49:48.230 --> 00:49:49.590
<v Allen>This is my son.
<v Allen>这是我儿子。

00:49:49.590 --> 00:49:51.030
<v David>Ah, what's his name?
<v David>啊，他叫什么名字？

00:49:51.030 --> 00:49:56.400
<v Allen>His name is [BLEEP] And then here's my daughter.
<v Allen>他叫[哔]。然后这是我女儿。

00:49:56.400 --> 00:49:59.060
<v David>Beautiful. Gorgeous.
<v David>漂亮。美极了。

00:49:59.060 --> 00:50:00.570
<v Allen>We're just getting to know each other.
<v Allen>我们才刚开始了解彼此。

00:50:00.570 --> 00:50:02.780
<v David>Yeah, gorgeous.
<v David>对，美极了。

00:50:02.780 --> 00:50:04.150
<v Allen>Beautiful kids.
<v Allen>漂亮的孩子。

00:50:04.150 --> 00:50:05.750
<v David>Whose dog is that?
<v David>那是谁的狗？

00:50:05.750 --> 00:50:27.710
<v M. Gessen>Beautiful kids, beautiful poodle, beautiful life. The only problem is Priscilla. Surely, after seeing these photos, David would see what a great father Allen was. Surely, he would feel even better about helping Allen get rid of the fly in the ointment. But David has a question. What is this going to do to the kids emotionally?
<v M. Gessen>漂亮的孩子，漂亮的贵宾犬，美好的生活。唯一的问号是普莉西拉。当然，看了这些照片后，大卫会看出艾伦是个多么伟大的父亲。当然，对于帮艾伦除掉这个绊脚石，他会感觉更好了。但大卫有一个问题。这会对孩子们的情绪造成什么影响？

00:50:27.710 --> 00:50:41.790
<v David>How do we protect the kids? I guess they're too young too. They're young too. But how do we-- how do we protect the kids? Look, they're going to lose their mother, right? She's fucking gone. How do we protect the kids?
<v David>我们怎么保护孩子？我猜他们也太小了。他们也很小。但我们怎么——我们怎么保护孩子？听着，他们要失去母亲了，对吧？她他妈的没了。我们怎么保护孩子？

00:50:41.790 --> 00:50:44.070
<v Allen>As long as they're not witness to violence.
<v Allen>只要他们没亲眼目睹暴力。

00:50:44.070 --> 00:50:48.790
<v M. Gessen>"As long as they're not witness to violence." That's the word he used. Violence.
<v M. Gessen>“只要他们没亲眼目睹暴力。”这是他用的词。暴力。

00:50:48.790 --> 00:51:14.910
<v David>No. They're not. They won't be. Yeah, they won't be. I mean, she'll be taken out without them present. Then I guess you can explain how you explain it. But just know that now that I'm seeing pictures of that, I just want to make sure that they're OK. I got a heart, too. Like I fucking-- don't get me wrong, I'll flip the light switch when I need to. But when I look at those kids like that, they're beautiful to me. I just want to make sure they're OK.
<v David>不。他们不会的。他们不会的。对，他们不会的。我的意思是，她会在他们不在场的情况下被带走。然后我想你可以解释你怎么解释。但要知道，现在我看到了这些照片，我只想确保他们没事。我也有心。就像我他妈的——别误会我，需要的时候我能翻脸不认人。但当我看着这样的孩子时，我觉得他们很美。我只想确保他们没事。

00:51:14.910 --> 00:51:35.350
<v M. Gessen>The undercover agent is methodical. He keeps coming closer to saying "she will be killed." And he keeps pushing Allen to consider the hypothetical stakes. The children will lose their mother forever. Allen blithely keeps incriminating himself. As long as the kids wouldn't see the murder happen, he didn't have other concerns.
<v M. Gessen>这位卧底特工很有条理。他一步步接近说出“她会被杀”。他不断敦促艾伦考虑假设中的利害关系。孩子们将永远失去母亲。艾伦却轻率地不断自证其罪。只要孩子们看不到谋杀的过程，他就没有别的顾虑了。

00:51:35.350 --> 00:51:41.870
<v M. Gessen>They wrap up their meeting. Allen has a plane to catch. The undercover agent has a lot to work with.
<v M. Gessen>他们的会面结束了。艾伦要赶飞机。卧底特工有很多材料可以利用。

00:51:41.870 --> 00:51:56.830
<v David>This is UC 4735, and today is Thursday, June 2, 2022. And this is the conclusion of a recorded conversation with Allen Gessen.
<v David>这是UC 4735，今天是2022年6月2日，星期四。这是与艾伦·盖森录音对话的结束。

00:51:56.830 --> 00:52:01.150
<v Ira Glass>So that all sounds very damning and very conclusive.
<v Ira Glass>所以这一切听起来都非常罪证确凿，非常具有决定性。

00:52:01.150 --> 00:52:39.290
<v M. Gessen>Yeah and then a few other people testified against Allen, including Priscilla. And then Allen took the stand, which is also very unusual for a criminal trial. Usually people don't testify in their own defense, and he tried to convince the jury that he had only wanted Priscilla deported, and that he did not want her killed. And so he went through with his attorney all those exchanges on tape and on text, trying to argue that all of them were just sort of vocabulary misunderstandings.
<v M. Gessen>对，然后还有其他几个人针对艾伦出庭作证，其中包括普莉西拉。接着艾伦出庭作证了，这在刑事审判中也非常罕见。通常人们不会为自己出庭作证，他试图说服陪审团，他当时只想把普莉西拉驱逐出境，而不想杀她。于是他和他的律师一起过了一遍录音和短信中的那些对话，试图辩称所有这些都只是一种词汇上的误解。

00:52:39.290 --> 00:52:41.950
<v Ira Glass>And that they were just misunderstanding each other somehow.
<v Ira Glass>并且他们只是不知怎么地互相误解了对方。

00:52:41.950 --> 00:52:44.390
<v M. Gessen>They were just talking at cross purposes.
<v M. Gessen>他们只是鸡同鸭讲。

00:52:44.390 --> 00:52:47.830
<v Ira Glass>And so how does it go over with the jury?
<v Ira Glass>那陪审团买账吗？

00:52:47.830 --> 00:53:21.710
<v M. Gessen>The jury doesn't buy it. The jury convicted him pretty fast of murder for hire. And then almost a whole year later, he was finally sentenced. And at the sentencing hearing, his lawyer again tried to say that he was only trying to get Priscilla deported, at which point, the judge said, you know, that crime that you're describing is actually called kidnapping, and it's punishable by up to 20 years in prison. So maybe just stop. And then she sentenced him to the maximum, which is 10 years in prison.
<v M. Gessen>陪审团不买账。陪审团很快就裁定他雇凶杀人罪名成立。然后差不多整整一年后，他终于被判刑。在量刑听证会上，他的律师再次试图辩称他当时只是想把普莉西拉驱逐出境，此时法官说，你知道，你所描述的那种罪行其实叫绑架，最高可判处20年监禁。所以也许还是闭嘴吧。然后她判处了他最高刑期，即10年监禁。

